      "math_academy_id": "q-182609",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,C\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C\\,$ | $\\,¬C∧(A∨C)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C{{field-4}}¬C∧(A∨C)\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $C≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬C∧(A∨C) & ≡¬\\text{T}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $C≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬C∧(A∨C) & ≡¬\\text{F}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $C≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C & ≡¬(¬\\text{F}∧¬\\text{T})∧¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡¬(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,C\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C\\,$ | $\\,¬C∧(A∨C)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C$ is logically equivalent to $¬C∧(A∨C),$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.  \n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(¬A∧¬C)∧¬C≡¬C∧(A∨C).\n$$",
